summary:
- topic: Student and Superintendent Reports
  text: Student representative Angela Kabisa reported on school activities, including
    athletic playoffs, PSAT prep, and Homecoming week. Superintendent Matheney celebrated
    National Principals Month, praised the recent Educator Justice Conference, and
    introduced the new Director of Buildings & Grounds, Harold Blaney.
- topic: Mental Health Initiatives
  text: The board discussed mental health supports, including a family night at the
    high school and a district-wide virtual forum with partners like NAMI and the
    American Foundation for Suicide Prevention. The Superintendent highlighted the
    district's robust mental health staffing and plans to partner with a national
    organization to enhance suicide prevention efforts.
- topic: Elementary School Demographics and Rezoning
  text: The Superintendent presented data revealing significant demographic disparities
    across the five elementary schools, with Skillin Elementary having far higher
    percentages of students of color, economically disadvantaged students, and multilingual
    learners than schools like Small Elementary. This data prompted a board discussion
    on the need to resume the process of redrawing attendance zones to promote equity,
    with plans to engage an external consultant.
- topic: Community School Presentation
  text: The principal and director of the South Portland Middle School Community School
    presented on their successful model, which is one of only four in Maine. They
    detailed how the model integrates academics, health services, and family engagement
    to improve student outcomes like attendance, and proposed expanding the model
    district-wide with a sustainable funding structure.
- topic: In-School Health Services Data
  text: The Superintendent shared data from the in-school health clinics run by Greater
    Portland Health, which provided over 1,200 medical visits, 346 dental visits,
    and 479 behavioral health visits last year. The data showed a 59% increase in
    medical visits over the previous year, with a majority of services being utilized
    by multilingual learners.
- topic: Policy Updates and Approvals
  text: The board approved several policies on second read, including those for Automated
    External Defibrillators (AEDs), job descriptions, and student suspension. They
    also rescinded several redundant library-related policies and held a first read
    for new policies on pest management and community use of facilities.
- topic: Public Comment and Board Elections
  text: During the open discussion, Board Member Rosemarie DeAngelis announced her
    candidacy for re-election in District 3. She also informed the public about a
    write-in candidate, Adrian Dowling, for the open District 5 seat, providing instructions
    on how to cast a valid write-in vote.
